WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.500
Hi, my name is Jordan Shamir with IBM Cloud

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.900
and today I'm going to be talking about Veeam.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:10.780
Veeam is an intelligent data management backup
and disaster recovery solution

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.840
that is focused on providing hyper availability

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.760
and uptime for their customers.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.840
Back up and disaster recovery is no longer a luxury,

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.740
but an absolute necessity.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.660
Our consumers expect us to stay online,

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.840
they want to be able to access our products when they want it.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.360
However, this is becoming much more challenging

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.020
with the rise of disasters such as natural disasters,

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.580
the rise of ransomware and cyberattacks,

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.380
and lastly human errors.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:41.820
Maintaining this uptime and availability is
becoming much, much more challenging.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:47.060
Many businesses have their disaster recovery
and backup environment within their own data center.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.300
This is risky because if your data center
goes down,

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.580
you are down.

00:00:51.589 --> 00:00:54.020
So, as companies begin to modernize,

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:58.400
they look at their cloud to provide a disaster recovery and backup environment.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.420
Some of the benefits are the geographic spread.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:06.060
We're giving you that two hundred, four hundred,
five hundred mile difference

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.680
to ensure availability by a different region.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:13.430
Also, beyond that we provide a variety of
different economic benefits because you don't

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:17.770
need a disaster recovery environment until
you're going for a test or an outage.

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:22.310
So, within the cloud you can use the flexibility
to have a low initial foot print and scale

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:26.290
up as needed to accommodate an outage.

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:30.740
Back up and disaster recovery is completely
different than availability.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:35.510
Cloud service providers guarantee you a certain
level of availability of your workloads, but

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:39.860
it doesn't mean that your workloads are backed
up and resilient.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:43.840
Whether in your own data center, cloud, or
a multicloud environment you need disaster

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:45.770
recovery and backup.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:49.270
Veeam on IBM Cloud is one option.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:54.160
Within IBM Cloud we give you full Bare Metal
and Hypervisor Access, and this is important

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:58.870
because it significantly reduces the learning
curve of using the cloud.

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:04.790
This enables you to maintain the same security,
flexibility, and control that you're running

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.790
in your own data center today.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.950
Specifically, with Veeam you get access to
all the advanced functionality which really

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.920
makes Veeam, Veeam.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:19.890
Such as Instant VM Recovery, SureReplica,
SureBackup and a variety of other features.

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:25.050
It's critical that businesses have deployment
flexibility as their requirements vary by

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:28.220
specific applications and workloads.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:32.850
In IBM Cloud we have over thirteen thousand
different deployments of Veeam.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:38.490
You can either deploy on our Virtual Server
Instances, are Non-Virtualized Bare Betal,

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:42.450
as well as our VMware and SAP workloads.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:46.540
These deployment options are available in
sixty plus data centers around the globe.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:51.670
One of the really cool things as you can actually
replicate between these data centers for free

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:52.670
and securely.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:58.020
So, if I think about backing up my own workloads,
I have my production data center in A, and

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:03.959
then my backup data center in B. So, replicating
between the two is completely free and secure

00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:05.810
within the IBM Cloud.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:10.530
And this really saves me a significant amount
of networking cost to have a backup and disaster

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:12.860
recovery environment in the cloud.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:18.550
In order to meet your consumer expectation
and availability requirements you need a multicloud

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:19.600
strategy.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:25.900
Veeam on IBM cloud provides you the control,
flexibility, and availability to meet your

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.090
business objectives.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:31.970
Thank you for watching if you have any questions
please comment below.

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:35.940
If you would like to learn more about what
IBM Cloud is doing, please subscribe to our

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:36.440
YouTube channel.

